## Summary

I implemented the native **SwiftUI/HIG `DigitalTwinPage`** at full web parity (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Vehicles/`), adaptive across macOS + iOS, and committed it (`0efc93a84`).

**Delivered (45/45 parity):**
- **5 glass panels** — twin visualization (reusing the shipped `VehicleTwinView` Canvas illustration), doors, windows, security & status, and the no-vehicles empty panel.
- **3 data states** (loading/empty/success, + error/retry) for every source.
- **All 37 web i18n keys** added to `Localizable.xcstrings` (+15 page/nav extras, en+ar+he) — zero hardcoded strings.
- `@Observable DigitalTwinPageModel` binding the four web hooks (`useVehicles`, `useVehicleState`, `useSecurityLatest`, `useChargingTelemetryLatest`) through a `DigitalTwinPageSource` seam (the established P4 pattern), reusing `TwinStateBuilder` so the projection matches `lib/vehicleState.ts`.
- New `.digitalTwin` route + registration; toolbar vehicle selector; SI display boundary; ADR-013 staleness; VoiceOver/Dynamic Type.

